{"version":"1","id":"unity","handle":"unity","name":"Unity","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/9afe038cc27e4d95ad581284cea8578d","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-4.4315,"y":2.4286,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":352,"newest_post_at":"2026-05-06T15:06:53.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2022-04-08T19:17:25.605Z","features":{"hype_score":0.00142,"listicle_ratio":0.051136,"question_ratio":0.002841,"avg_read_time":4.911932,"summary_length_avg":412.128125,"title_length_avg":53.323864,"title_length_var":299.145112,"tag_entropy":2.76869,"tag_diversity":0.284091,"top_tag_share":0.130682,"avg_upvotes":2.579545,"median_upvotes":1.0,"avg_comments":0.153409,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.060506,"zero_engagement_share":0.46875,"viral_share":0.002841,"posts_per_week":1.654991,"non_article_ratio":0.318182,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.530435},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[0.9853,5.5735],"cadence_depth":[7.25,-2.6471],"hype_variety":[-3.5588,-4.2206],"title_style":[-3.5735,8.2794]},"top_tags":[["unity",312],["game-development",182],["gaming",40],["vr",28],["performance",22],["3d",18],["ai",18],["ar",13]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Our first-ever guide about animation in Unity","Inside the Survival Kids Multiplayer Network Architecture","Games made with Unity: June 2025 in review"],"outlier":["Unity 6 tips: URP settings for mobile #gamedev #unitytips #unity3d #unitylearn #3dgamedevelopment"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"t7AAErPgj","title":"Unity AI Open Beta | Launch Trailer","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pHRZm2BwNQc","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/unity-ai-open-beta-launch-trailer-t7aaerpgj","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/pHRZm2BwNQc/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-04T15:00:19.000Z"},{"id":"jog16WBjs","title":"Unity Studio - Working with Materials","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kANjVPFCUkQ","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/unity-studio---working-with-materials-jog16wbjs","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/kANjVPFCUkQ/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-01T19:44:07.000Z"},{"id":"LxvXNqPtw","title":"Games made with Unity: April 2026 in review","url":"https://unity.com/blog/games-made-with-unity-april-2026-releases","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/games-made-with-unity-april-2026-in-review-lxvxnqptw","summary":"A curated roundup of games released on Steam in April 2026 that were built with Unity. Highlights include 1.0 launches like MOUSE: P.I. For Hire and Vampire Crawlers: The Turbo Wildcard from Vampire Survivors, early access entries such as Heroes of Might and Magic: Olden Era and Morbid Metal, and recognition of Unity developers who won awards at the 2026 BAFTA Games Awards. The full list spans dozens of titles across genres including action, roguelike, strategy, simulation, puzzle, and more.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f2e48be106d6adaecb35d8364e333342?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-01T13:53:21.569Z"},{"id":"Y22AwIt8Y","title":"Unity Studio \u2013 Animating Your Scene: Motion & Effects","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gmA1f1YMbsA","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/unity-studio-animating-your-scene-motion-effects-y22awit8y","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/gmA1f1YMbsA/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-29T15:46:41.000Z"},{"id":"M8OrBanMB","title":"CTV and mobile gaming: How brands are closing the second-screen gap","url":"https://unity.com/blog/capturing-second-screen-attention-with-ctv-and-mobile-gaming","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ctv-and-mobile-gaming-how-brands-are-closing-the-second-screen-gap-m8orbanmb","summary":"Second-screen behavior during TV viewing is fragmenting advertiser attention, and brands are increasingly pairing Connected TV (CTV) campaigns with mobile gaming placements to recapture it. The post outlines three use cases: extending live sports sponsorships into gaming moments, reinforcing back-to-school campaigns by targeting parents during nighttime gaming sessions, and amplifying trailer bursts across both screens. The argument is that today's gaming audience is mainstream \u2014 parents, professionals, decision-makers \u2014 making mobile gaming a natural complement to CTV buys rather than a niche add-on. Unity positions its combined CTV and gaming solutions as the way to measure and act on cross-screen attention.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/21f8890a3c471bf23531a6d393bdb0cb?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-28T20:31:39.782Z"},{"id":"a8ecnzI9b","title":"Unity 6 Tips: Decal Renderer Feature #UnityTips #GameDev","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-HrYyWU736k","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/unity-6-tips-decal-renderer-feature-unitytips-gamedev-a8ecnzi9b","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/-HrYyWU736k/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-28T20:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"FzKLjh5U6","title":"2D Beginner Adventure: Robot Repair","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LgWQy6UWM9g","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/2d-beginner-adventure-robot-repair-fzkljh5u6","summary":"Robot Repair is a beginner-friendly Unity course for 2D game development, updated for Unity 6.3. It walks learners through building a complete 2D adventure game step-by-step, covering player movement, world building, hazards, collectibles, enemies, UI, game loops, dialogue, scripting, audio, and visual effects. The course offers multiple visual style asset packs for customization and includes a playable demo on Unity Play.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/LgWQy6UWM9g/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-27T18:27:40.000Z"},{"id":"Y6nsalE0I","title":"The tech behind IGF winner Titanium Court","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CyA_jXfKZag","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-tech-behind-igf-winner-titanium-court-y6nsale0i","summary":"A deep dive into the narrative design system behind Titanium Court, an IGF-winning game blending match-three, tower defense, resource management, and roguelike elements. The developer explains a 'storylit' system where individual scenes are authored as self-contained JSON files containing dialogue, stage directions, and metadata about when and under what conditions they trigger. A Unity editor pre-processor converts these JSON files into prefabs indexed by a central object that dynamically selects scenes based on game state. The approach enables modular, reactive storytelling but trades off a clear linear narrative bible for flexibility.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/CyA_jXfKZag/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-24T14:00:30.000Z"},{"id":"EvvTAnBLs","title":"Getting Started with Awaitables","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eXkFPoEp3BA","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/getting-started-with-awaitables-evvtanbls","summary":"A beginner-to-intermediate guide to Unity's Awaitable system, covering how to replace coroutine patterns with async/await. Topics include awaiting time delays (WaitForSeconds equivalent), frame-based waits, async asset loading, thread switching between main and background threads, wiring cancellation tokens to Unity object lifetimes, and avoiding the pooled-awaitable pitfall by converting to Tasks for multi-await scenarios.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/eXkFPoEp3BA/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-23T17:01:00.000Z"},{"id":"u2GLIbm8l","title":"Making fire feel alive: Real-time fluid simulation in Ignitement","url":"https://unity.com/blog/real-time-fluid-simulation-fire-vfx-ignitement-breakdown","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/making-fire-feel-alive-real-time-fluid-simulation-in-ignitement-u2glibm8l","summary":"Solo developer S\u00f8rb details the real-time 2D fluid simulation powering fire and lava VFX in the upcoming action roguelite Ignitement, built entirely in Unity. The system runs via Graphics.Blit on a small set of textures (density, velocity, temperature, reaction) using fragment shaders instead of compute shaders for broad hardware compatibility. Fire rendering uses a parallax trick for pseudo-3D depth, embers are GPU-driven particles sampling the velocity field, and a downsampled reaction texture doubles as a dynamic light map affecting environment shaders and UI. Crucially, the reaction texture is read back to the CPU each frame via AsyncGPUReadback to drive gameplay damage logic, making fire a true gameplay mechanic. Key trade-offs include a 2D-only simulation and a camera-following domain to keep costs low while maintaining the illusion of a continuous world.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/24ca87ba61c36f39225ac0ff21471bc0?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-23T12:41:06.643Z"}],"similar_handles":["codehead","moralis","bradfrost","uxplanet","ionic"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","hamelhusain","tbpn","alexfinn","xai"],"similar":[{"id":"codehead","handle":"codehead","name":"CodeHead","is_squad":false,"x":-4.5773,"y":2.5247,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":166,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ywzrIEkA--/f_auto/v1745508579/logos/codehead","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":3.115306,"median_upvotes":3.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.027108,"avg_read_time":4.301205,"tag_diversity":0.873494},"top_tags_preview":[["webdev",49],["career",36],["devops",21]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[9.0588,8.0294],"cadence_depth":[2.1765,-3.9853],"hype_variety":[6.2794,8.7794],"title_style":[4.1324,6.6618]}},{"id":"moralis","handle":"moralis","name":"Moralis","is_squad":false,"x":-4.6214,"y":2.